<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eudokia Angelina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eudokia Angelina was a daughter of the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-iii-angelos">Alexios III Angelos</a>. She was first married to the Serbian prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-the-first-crowned">Stefan Nemanjić</a> and, after their separation, to Alexios V Doukas, briefly emperor during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>. After his fall she married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-sgouros">Leo Sgouros</a>, the lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a> and Corinth, who gained from the match a measure of legitimacy.</p></div>
